course: dictionary
lesson: 9531
title: One word, many meanings: stir
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word stir has more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. Look at the other words in the sentence. «The Duchess, nursing a howling baby, and a cook stirring soup» tells you that stirring soup means moving a spoon round and round to mix it.
explain: Stir can also mean to move a little. «The baby stirred in her sleep» does not mean a spoon was used. The words in her sleep are the clue: the baby moved slightly, but did not wake up fully.
explain: Stir can describe a feeling or a mood. «Grief... can be stirred up again by a house, a date, a song» means strong feelings come back. Stir up means cause trouble or strong feelings. When you meet stir, ask: does a spoon fit here, or does a feeling or a crowd fit better? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Stir is a verb (stir, stirs, stirred, stirring) and a noun (a stir).
fact: To stir means to move a spoon or stick round and round in a liquid to mix it.
fact: «The baby stirred in her sleep» means the baby moved slightly.
fact: A stir is excitement or trouble among people: «The news caused a stir.»
fact: Stir up means to cause trouble or strong feelings, and «stirring up trouble» means causing arguments on purpose.
exercise: «A cook was stirring the soup in the big pot.» What does stirring mean here? | Sleeping quietly | Freezing solid | Shouting loudly | *Moving a spoon round and round to mix
exercise: «The news caused a stir in the village.» What is a stir here? | *Excitement and talk among people | A small wooden spoon | A quiet, peaceful sleep
exercise: «The baby stirred in her sleep.» What does stirred mean here? | Ate a big dinner | *Moved slightly | Stopped breathing | Ran out of the room
test: «Grief can be stirred up again by a song.» What does stirred up mean? | Forgotten for ever | Washed away completely | Cooked in a pan | *Brought back strong feelings
test: «Ice cream is stirred while freezing so the ice crystals stay tiny.» Why is it stirred? | To stop it from being made | *To mix it evenly so the crystals stay small | To turn it into a hot drink | To make the crystals grow big
exam: «Pau Amma can only stir up the sea.» Which meaning fits best? | Put sugar into the sea | *Cause a rough, churning disturbance | Sleep gently on the water | Stop the wind from blowing
